the simple fact here is that the saving sequence is hazardous, requiring
you to type "y" and "n" for a normal save. you're not the first nor will
you be the last person to "kill" a game in this manner. the save sequence
ought to be (while there's a choice):

Really Save? [ynx?]
y = yes, save as normal
n = no, continue playing game
x = save as an explore-mode only game
? = explain the above options

the "ynx?" keys are also nowhere adjacent to each other and the default
non-answer should be "y". explore-mode options should be presented in
the startup news, man pages, guidebook, on-line help etc. but should
not intrude in the play of the game.
